WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.701
Salzburg has plenty of beautiful things to
offer: mountains, a Baroque town centre, an

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:13.099
impressive medieval fortress - and one of
Austria's best-known shopping streets: Getreidegasse.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:20.949
Tour guide Inez Reichl has a few tips on where
the locals like to go.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:32.829
Café Classic, for instance.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:37.579
"The hot chocolate here is my favourite.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:41.629
The Café Classic is on the ground floor of
the house where Mozart lived.

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:43.450
Not many people know about it.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.559
It's a place locals enjoy - and I'm one of
them."

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:47.559
+++

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:51.960
The first floor of the building called the
Mozart Residence houses museum pieces.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.649
You can only touch the keys of these instruments
if you have special permission.

00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:02.280
"This is the Mozart family's old pianoforte.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.750
Wolfgang himself played on it."

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:10.720
Steingasse is also largely unknown to tourists,
even though it's in the oldest part of Salzburg.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.670
The first houses were built here in the 11th
century.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:20.469
These distinctive grooves are much newer.

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:27.970
"They were made after World War Two, when
the Americans were here in Salzburg.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:33.180
The GIs, the young soldiers, tried to drive
into this narrow lane with a tank, because

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.170
there was a brothel back there.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:43.250
Unfortunately, the GIs had had a few beers,
got stuck, and had to be towed out.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:49.060
People here found it so funny that they left
the marks."

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.020
The people of Salzburg aren't just proud of
their history.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:59.770
The Museum of Modern Art, at first a controversial
construction, has attracted thousands of visitors

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:05.130
since 2004.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:12.490
"First of all, its location is fantastic.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:16.040
From up here you have a great view over the
city.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.930
And then I think it's incredibly important
that in addition to the baroque, the old and

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:27.190
traditional, we have new things, and the museum
is the perfect place for that."

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:33.050
And here's a relaxing way to end your day
in Salzburg : in "M32," the restaurant in

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.050
the museum building.

